  id: W3_02
  era: c. 11th century
  title: Shiva Nataraja, Lord of the Dance
  text: Shiva Nataraja, Lord of the Dance. Shiva performs the cosmic dance that destroys and recreates the universe, framed by a ring of fire and trampling the dwarf of ignorance. Chola bronzes like this were carried in temple processions, dressed in silk and jewels. They are among the masterpieces of world metal sculpture. Each bronze was cast in a single piece using the lost-wax method, so no two are exactly alike. Bronze-casters in Swamimalai in Tamil Nadu still work the same way today.
  narration: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4be3d25abdfa14150b54611bcc7b6c8b, type: 3}
